Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:14:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(quiz): keep author on admin-created tests and answers
 (#542)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TestView and AnswerView left the created_by_user relation in their create
forms. flask-admin's populate_obj writes the blank field to the model and,
on flush, SQLAlchemy syncs the NULL relation over the created_by_id set in
on_model_change, so every Test/Answer created through the admin had no
author. created_by_formatter then raised for those rows and /admin/test/
and /admin/answer/ answered 500.

- exclude created_by_id/created_by_user from both forms (as SectionView and
  QuestionView already do);
- created_by_formatter renders '—' and logs a warning instead of raising,
  so rows already stored without an author no longer break the list pages.

Verified on a local stand (Flask-Admin 2.0.1, PostgreSQL 18): before - author
NULL and 500 on both list pages; after - author set, lists render.
Adds browser-free test_admin_author.py (registered in front_coverage.yml).
